+var description_default53 = "Hand your box's desktop to the user for a step a form cannot do: single sign-on through another company's sign-in page, a passkey, a captcha the subagent tried and could not get past, an approval on another app or device, a QR code, a bank or 3DS confirmation after the card is entered, a field the Secure Form host refused or reported a failed fill for, or a sign-in the user prefers to do themselves. It is the last step of the `sign-in` skill. A typed login, address, card, or one-time code goes to RequestUserForm first when it is among your tools, embedded and cross-origin fields included;
+ entering the card itself is the Secure Form. Hand off only when that tool is not offered, the step is not a typed field, or the host refused the form or reported a failed fill, and quote the host's reason as written. Pass one short instruction (no paragraph);
+ the box is surfaced with a \"hand back to agent\" button and that instruction is shown in chat, then your turn ends. The user does the step on the box and hands it back, and you are resumed automatically, so start by using the read-only Screenshot tool to see what they changed. When the user signs in on the box, you never see their password or code. For classification: domain is the destination app being accessed;
